#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 137.42pt, "Introduction. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 162.38pt, "Memristive devices are at the core of several emerging and commercially deployed ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 179.42pt, "microelectronic technologies and are expected to play a central role in the future ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 196.34pt, "integrated-circuit market [Lanza2022, Ielmini2015, Lanza2025]. Their most immediate ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 213.26pt, "impact is in non-volatile memory, where leading semiconductor companies—including ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 230.3pt, "TSMC and Intel—are directly incorporating memristive elements into advanced ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 247.22pt, "technology nodes for embedded and stand-alone memory solutions [Chiu2019, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 264.29pt, "Chou2018, Chou2020]. In parallel, neuromorphic engineering [Mead1989] is undergoing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 281.21pt, "rapid development, with memristive devices serving as artificial synapses in hardware ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 298.13pt, "neural networks designed to accelerate AI training and inference [Aguirre2024, Hui2021, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 315.17pt, "Danilin2015, ")
  #line-at(157.068pt, 315.17pt, "Mishchenko2022, ")
  #line-at(268.368pt, 315.17pt, "Perez-Bosch2021, ")
  #line-at(381.494pt, 315.17pt, "Yu2021, ")
  #line-at(442.418pt, 315.17pt, "Sebastian2020, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 332.09pt, "Prezioso2015, ")
  #line-at(158.76pt, 332.09pt, "Zhu2023, ")
  #line-at(221.232pt, 332.09pt, "Tang2019, ")
  #line-at(287.784pt, 332.09pt, "Romero-Zaliz2021, ")
  #line-at(400.114pt, 332.09pt, "Wang2020, ")
  #line-at(472.066pt, 332.09pt, "Milo2016, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 349.13pt, "Roldan2022]. Beyond memory and neuromorphic computing, memristive devices also ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 366.05pt, "play an increasingly important role in cryptographic systems: their inherent stochasticity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 382.97pt, "and device-to-device variability provide high-entropy sources for true random number ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 400.01pt, "generators and physical unclonable functions [Wei2016, Gao2022, Lanza2022, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 416.93pt, "Wen2021, Nili2018]. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 441.91pt, "Many memristive systems [Chua1971, Chua1976] exhibit resistive switching (RS), in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 458.95pt, "which the internal conductance can be reversibly modified by several orders of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 475.87pt, "magnitude under electrical stimulus. Resistive Random Access Memories (RRAM), a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 492.79pt, "widely studied subset of memristive devices [Chua2011], rely on ionic transport and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 509.83pt, "localized redox reactions to form and rupture conductive filaments (CFs) within ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 526.75pt, "insulating or semiconducting matrices [Spiga2020]. These mechanisms enable both ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 543.79pt, "digital (binary) operation for non-volatile memory and analog/multilevel operation, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 560.71pt, "essential for emulating synaptic weight updates in neuromorphic architectures ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 577.63pt, "[Tang2019, Roldan2022, Mishchenko2022, Maldonado2023]. Multilevel states can be ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 594.67pt, "programmed through voltage-pulse algorithms [Reuben2019, Perez-Bosch2021], ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 611.59pt, "compliance-current modulation [Gonzalez-Cordero2019, Poblador2018], or by ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 628.66pt, "exploiting quantum transport effects through nanometric constrictions in CFs ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 645.58pt, "[Milano2022, Roldan2023a]. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 670.54pt, "Conductance quantization is particularly attractive for multilevel memory and quantum-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 687.46pt, "inspired information processing. Under this regime, device conductance evolves in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 704.74pt, "discrete steps near integer or half-integer multiples of the quantum of conductance, ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.46pt, 704.74pt, "𝐺")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.52pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(505.66pt, 707.14pt, "0")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(514.42pt, 704.74pt, "=")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 721.9pt, "2𝑒")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.52pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.224pt, 717.46pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.624pt, 721.9pt, "/ℎ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(103.46pt, 721.9pt, ". Such behavior emerges when electrons travel ballistically through atomic-scale ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 738.82pt, "constrictions—conditions readily achievable in metallic CFs formed during RRAM ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 755.736pt, "switching [Miranda2001, Miranda2010]. Since the elastic mean free path of common ")
