#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-05.png", width: 323.5pt), 72pt, 625pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 83.28pt, "Conclusion. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 108.26pt, "Taken together, these works demonstrate the broad potential of Prussian Blue, Prussian ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 125.18pt, "White, and related hybrid materials as active layers in resistive switching and energy-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 142.22pt, "storage devices. Electrodeposited PB and PW films exhibit stable bipolar and unipolar RS ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 159.14pt, "behavior over hundreds of cycles, with conduction dominated by ionic motion primarily ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 176.18pt, "potassium ions and defect-mediated filamentary pathways located at grain boundaries. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 193.1pt, "The activation energies, ranging from 0.2 to 0.4 eV, confirm ion-driven transport, while ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 210.02pt, "endurance and retention tests show reliable long-term stability suitable for memory ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 227.06pt, "applications. Advanced analysis, including EIS and quantum transport modeling, reveals ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 243.98pt, "the formation of both nanoscale and atomic-scale conductive filaments, the latter ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 261.02pt, "responsible for conductance quantization at multiples of G₀, enabling multilevel memory ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 277.97pt, "capabilities. Variability studies further indicate that PB-based memristors possess ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 294.89pt, "sufficiently low cycle-to-cycle fluctuations for neuromorphic and cryptographic uses ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 311.93pt, "such as PUFs and true random number generation. The observed performance across ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 328.85pt, "devices combined with low-cost, CMOS-compatible electrodeposition, highlights PBAs ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 345.89pt, "as scalable platforms for both nonvolatile memory and secure electronics. Beyond RS ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 362.81pt, "devices, PB analogues integrated with reduced graphene oxide achieve high-voltage (2 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 379.73pt, "V), high-stability supercapacitor performance, demonstrating their versatility in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 396.77pt, "electrochemical energy storage. Complementary results from perylene-based liquid ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 413.69pt, "crystal systems expand the material space for organic memory devices, revealing stable ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 430.73pt, "RS behavior and long-term data retention enabled by reversible molecular reduction. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 447.67pt, "Overall, these findings establish Prussian Blue analogues and related materials as ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 464.59pt, "promising, multifunctional candidates for next-generation memory, neuromorphic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 481.63pt, "computing, secure hardware, and high-performance energy-storage technologies, while ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 498.55pt, "outlining clear pathways for future optimization in device architecture, environmental ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 515.59pt, "stability, and controlled ionic transport. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 565.51pt, "References. ")
